.TH smi-pki-create-domain-cert "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI PKI Command"
.SH NAME
smi-pki-create-domain-cert \- Create a server certificate signed by the Intermediate CA
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-pki-create-domain-cert
.I DIRECTORY
.I DOMAIN_NAME
.RI [ ROOT_DOMAIN ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-pki-create-domain-cert
generates a private key and a signed TLS server certificate for the specified \fIDOMAIN_NAME\fR,
for example \fBldap.has.ee.gintra\fR.
It requires that \fBsmi-pki-ca-create\fR(1) has already created the Root CA and Intermediate CA in
\fIDIRECTORY\fR.
The CA files are named by the root domain the CA was created with: \fIROOT_DOMAIN\fR when given,
otherwise \fIDOMAIN_NAME\fR with its first label removed.
The Intermediate CA is checked before anything is generated; when it is missing, the command names
the file it looked for, creates no files and exits with 1.
.PP
The process:
.IP 1.
Generates a 2048-bit RSA private key (mode \fB600\fR) and public key for the domain.
.IP 2.
Creates a CSR whose \fBsubjectAltName\fR is \fBDNS:\fIDOMAIN_NAME\fR, the exact host, no wildcard.
.IP 3.
Signs the CSR with the \fBIntermediate\fR CA key and certificate from the \fBca\fR subdirectory,
never with the Root CA.
.IP 4.
The certificate is \fBCA:FALSE\fR with critical \fBkeyUsage\fR
\fBdigitalSignature,keyEncipherment\fR, \fBextendedKeyUsage=serverAuth\fR, and the same
\fBsubjectAltName\fR, so clients validate the host from the SAN rather than the Common Name.
It is valid for 825 days.
.PP
The domain key, CSR and certificate are written in \fIDIRECTORY\fR itself, outside the \fBca\fR
subdirectory.
Because the certificate chains to the Root CA through the Intermediate CA, a client that trusts the
Root CA trusts it without any per-certificate installation.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I DIRECTORY
PKI directory: the CA files are read from its \fBca\fR subdirectory, the server files are written
into it.
.TP
.I DOMAIN_NAME
Host name of the server certificate, used as Common Name and \fBsubjectAltName\fR.
.TP
.I ROOT_DOMAIN
Root domain given to \fBsmi-pki-ca-create\fR(1), which selects
\fBca/\fIROOT_DOMAIN\fB.intermediate.crt\fR and \fB.intermediate.priv.key\fR.
Optional; needed whenever the CA root domain is not \fIDOMAIN_NAME\fR minus its first label, for
example a CA created for \fBgintra\fR and a server \fBsetmy.info.gintra\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
CA created for \fBhas.ee.gintra\fR, root domain derived from the host name:
.RS
.nf
smi-pki-create-domain-cert /var/opt/pki ldap.has.ee.gintra
.fi
.RE
.PP
CA created for \fBgintra\fR, a host two labels below it:
.RS
.nf
smi-pki-ca-create /var/opt/pki gintra true
smi-pki-create-domain-cert /var/opt/pki setmy.info.gintra gintra
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The certificate was created.
.TP
.B 1
Wrong usage, the Intermediate CA was not found, or an OpenSSL step failed.
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
.SH "REPORTING BUGS"
.PP
Report smi-pki-create-domain-cert bugs to \fIinfo@setmy.info\fR
